# Google OAuth2 credentials for Google Drive integration
# Create OAuth Client IDs at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#
# Copy this to `src-tauri/.env`, not to the repository root. `dotenvy` searches
# upward and would find either, but `build.rs` declares
# `cargo:rerun-if-changed=.env` relative to the crate — so a root-level copy is
# read once and then never watched, and editing it does not rebuild anything.
#
# Two clients are needed, because Google will not let one cover both cases.

# ── Desktop (macOS, Windows, Linux) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Client type: Desktop app.
# The desktop flow redirects to http://127.0.0.1:<port>, and Google still
# requires client_secret on the token endpoint for this client type — PKCE is
# layered on top rather than instead.
SYNABIT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-desktop-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
SYNABIT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-desktop-client-secret-here

# ── Android ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Client type: Android. Required — the build fails without it, on purpose.
#
# The mobile flow redirects to com.synabit.app:/oauth2callback, the package name
# as a custom scheme, and Google accepts a custom-scheme redirect only from a
# client of type Android. Pointing this at the desktop client ID produces a
# build that works everywhere except on a phone, where every "Connect Google
# Drive" ends in invalid_request.
#
# Registering it asks for the package name and a SHA-1 signing fingerprint:
#
#   Package name: com.synabit.app
#
# Register BOTH fingerprints, as two separate Android clients or one client per
# key, whichever the console offers:
#
#   1. The upload key — what you sign with locally and what CI uploads:
#        keytool -list -v -keystore src-tauri/gen/android/synabit-release-key.jks \
#                -alias <keyAlias>
#
#   2. The Play App Signing key — what Google re-signs with before distributing.
#      Different from the upload key, and it is the one that matters on a user's
#      phone. Play Console → your app → Test and release → Setup → App signing.
#
# Registering only the upload key gives you a sideloaded build where Drive works
# and a Play build where it does not.
#
# No client secret: an Android client is a public client and PKCE carries it.
SYNABIT_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=your-android-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
